$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Experimental Procedure for the O-Arylation
using Cs2CO3 as a Mild Base (Table 3). To an oven-dried screwed vial were
added bromoarene (0.2 mmol), phenols (0.3 mmol), cesium carbonate (130
mg, 0.4 mmol), Rh(cod)(iPr-bimy)Br (4.5 mg, 5 mol %), AgSbF6 (7 mg, 10
mol %), toluene (0.2 mL), and Et3N (0.2 mL). The mixture was vigorously
stirred at 100 °C for 24 h and diluted with ethyl acetate. The crude
reaction mixture was filtered through a pad of silica gel and organic
solvents were removed in vacuo, and then it was purified by silica gel
column chromatography (ethyl acetate/n-hexane).
4-(4-Ethylphenoxy)benzonitrile (3q, Table 3). The title compound was
purified by silica gel column chromatography (EtOAc/n-Hx, 1:10). pale
yellow oil (31 mg, 70%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.57-7.54 (2H, m),
7.23-7.20 (2H, m), 6.98-6.94 (4H, m), 2.67 (2H, q, J = 7.6), 1.25 (3H, m,
J = 7.5 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 162.0, 152.4, 141.2, 134.0,
129.4, 120.3, 118.9, 117.5, 105.4, 28.2, 15.6; IR (Film) ν 2966, 2872,
2226, 1597, 1499, 1455, 1416, 1286, 1249, 1201, 874, 835, 544 cm-1; HRMS
(EI+) m/z calcd. for C15H13NO [M]+: 208.0757, found: 223.0997.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 5 mol% Rh-NHC catalyst; 10 mol% silver salt
