$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Reaction Conditions for the synthesis
of diazadioxacalix[4]arenes 5: Under ambient atmosphere, an air-dried
flask was charged with nucleophile 2 (0.50 mmol, 1 equiv) and
electrophile 1 (204 mg, 1.0 mmol, 2 equiv). DMF (2.0 mL) was added,
followed by (iPr)2NEt (0.400 mL, 2.4 mmol, 4.7 equiv for 2b-2d; 0.600 mL,
3.5 mmol, 7.0 equiv for 2a used as its bis-hydrochloride salt), and the
reaction was stirred for 2 h at 25 °C. Diphenol 4 (0.50 mmol, 1 equiv)
was then added, and the reaction was heated to 60 °C and allowed to stir
for an additional 2 h. The reaction was cooled to room temperature, and
then the product precipitated by the addition of 0.5 M HCl (10.0 mL).
Unpurified 5 was then isolated by vacuum filtration, washed with water
(10.0 mL) and dried in vacuo. The product was then purified by flash
chromatography as described below.
10-methoxy-23-methyl-4,6,16,18-tetranitro-8,14-diaza-2,20-dioxacalix[4]arene
(5b): 1, 2a, and 4b were condensed under the General Reaction Conditions
for the synthesis of diazadioxacalix[4]arenes 5, and the product purified
via flash column chromatography through silica (gradient 0-3% CH3CN in
CH2Cl2) to yield 207 mg 5a as a yellow-orange solid (70%). 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.69 (s, 1H), 9.54 (s, 1H), 9.14 (s, 1H), 9.13 (s, 1H),
7.14-7.11 (m, 2H), 7.06 (d, 1H, J = 8.8 Hz), 6.91 (t, 1H, J = 2.0 Hz),
6.85 (t, 1H, J = 2.0 Hz), 6.78 (t, 1H, J = 2.0 Hz), 6.10 (s, 1H), 6.04
(s, 1H), 3.90 (s, 3H), 2.37 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 158.2,
158.0, 153.8, 153.5, 153.4, 147.9, 146.9, 144.0, 129.4, 129.4, 127.9,
127.8, 127.1, 126.9, 126.8, 125.9, 124.4, 120.6, 120.5, 113.5, 111.7,
100.4, 99.8, 56.2, 21.4; IR (ATR) 3317, 3090, 2928, 2843, 1614, 1571,
1506, 1420, 1331, 1291, 1259, 1236, 1119, 1058, 1020, 831, 734 cm-1; HRMS
[MALDI(-) with a DHB matrix] calculated for (M-H)- [C26H18N6O11]-:
589.09608, found: 589.0961.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
