$DATUM 67-68-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step a A mixture of 1-fluoro-3-iodo-5-nitrobenzene (5.0 g, 18.0 mmol),
2-methoxyphenol (2.3 g, 18.0 mmol) in dry DMSO (10.0 mL) and anhydrous
K2CO3 (3.8 g, 27.5 mmol) was heated at 110 °C for 16 h. The mixture was
poured into ice water and extracted with EtOAc (3 x 50 mL). The organic
layer was sequentially washed with brine (2 x 75 mL), dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4, concentrated by rotary evaporation, and purified by
column chromatography to give 1-iodo-3-(2-methoxyphenoxy)-5-nitrobenzene
(7) Yield 4.7g, 70%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.23 - 8.13 (m, 1H), 7.69
-7.48 (m, 2H), 7.30 - 7.25 (m, 1H), 7.12 - 6.93 (m, 3H), 3.80 (d, J=1.9
Hz, 3H).
