$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.2 Coupling of iodide (C-1) with
hydroxybenzaldehydes and brominated Methoxyphenols:
2,2',4,4'-Tetrabromodiphenyliodonium iodide (C-1) (3.0 mmol) was added to
a solution of the brominated methoxyphenol (C-2~5) and
hydroxybenzaldehyde (C-6~7) (2.5 mmol), 18-crown-6 and suspended K2CO3
(5.0 mmol) in N,N-dimethyl acetamide (DMAC), and the reaction mixture was
stirred at 80 °C for 1.5 h. The mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 and water
was added. The organic layer was separated and the water layer was
extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were washed with
aqueous NaHSO3 (5%), aqueous NaOH (1 mol/L), and water. The purification
of the final products was performed on a silica gel with n-hexane/ethyl
acetate (dichloromethane) as eluent. Generally, the volume ratio of
n-hexane/dichloromethane is 1/2~3/1 and n-hexane/ethyl acetate is mainly
6.0. MeO-4, yield 70%. Mp = 140-141 δC. MS/(m/z)= 516 [M+4]+ (83),
Rel/int% = 356 [M-2Br]+(100). Chemical shift of H (δ/10-6) 3.79/MeO,
6.49, 6.64, 7.36, 7.79, 7.79.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of hydroxylated and methoxylated polybrominated diphenyl ethers
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zheng, Ke-wen; Gao, Li-ping; Cao, Jie; Yu, Hai-wen; Zhang, Zhang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Shanghai University (2009), 13(1), 81-87

