$DATUM 14. A solution of 13 (840 mg, 2.29 mmol) and 9 (1.37 g, 2 equiv) in DMSO
(25 mL) under Ar was treated with 18-c-6 (3.0 g, 5 equiv), 4 A molecular
sieves (1 g), and K2CO3 (1.9 g, δ equiv). The mixture was stirred at 25
°C overnight before the dark mixture was poured into H2O (100 mL) and
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 50 mL). The organic phases were combined,
washed with saturated aqueous NaCl3 dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
concentrated. Flash chromatography (SiO2, 5 x 15 cm, 50% EtOAc-hexanes)
provided 14 (1.03 g, 1.47 g theoretical, 70%) as a yellow foam. [α]25D
+45 (c 1.8, CHCl3); 1H NMR (CDCl3,400 MHz) S 8.07 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H),
7.91 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.15 (dd, J = 1.5, 8.5 Hz, 1H), 7.00 (d, J =
1.4 Hz, 1H), 6.63 (s, 1H), 6.53 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 2H), 3.99 (dd, J = 7.9,
10.6 Hz, 1H), 3.77 (s, 4H), 3.75-3.63 (m, 4H), 3.62-3.54 (m, 2H), 3.51
(s, 3H), 2.94 (s, 1H), 1.37 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 161.3,
157.4, 157.3 (q, J = 39.4 Hz), 155.5, 150.1, 140.5, 140.1, 125.9, 121.9,
119.3, 117.2, 109.3, 108.7, 104.3, 94.8, 80.1, 71.8, 68.6, 65.0, 58.7,
55.8, 55.5, 53.9, 28.2 (3C); IR (film) νmax 3319, 3078, 2934, 1717, 1608,
1588, 1559, 1525, 1489, 1457, 1436, 1392, 1350, 1293, 1247, 1163, 1052
cm-1; MALDIFTMS (DHB) m/z 670.2204 (M+ + Na, C28H36F3N3O11 requires 670.2
194).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
