$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (2-nitro-phenyl)-phenyl ether (3a)
(2-nitro-phenyl)-(2,6-di-iso-propyllphenyl) ether (3d). Following above
procedure, 2,6-di- iso-proyllphenol (3.56 g, 20mmol), KOH (1.12 g,
20mmol) and 1-chloro-2-nitro-benzene ( 3.15 g, 20 mmol) were used. 3d
(4.2 g) was obtained as a yellow powder in 70 % yield. 1H NMR (300MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.95 (dd, 1H, J = 1.5, 8.1 Hz, Ar-H ), 7.38-7.21 (m, 4H, Ar-H),
7.04 (t, 1H, J = 8.4 Hz, Ar-H), 6.54 (d, 1H, J = 8.4 Hz, Ar-H), 2.97
(hepta, 2H, J = 6.6 Hz, CH(CH3)2), 1.21(d, 6H, J = 6.9 Hz, CH(CH3)2),
1.09 (d, 6H, J = 6.9 Hz, CH(CH3)2).
