$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 1262046-34-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction Conditions Table 1 in the Manuscript
An oven-dried test tube, which was equipped with a magnetic stir bar and
fitted with a teflon screwcup, was charged with ligand (4 mol %, 0.008
mmol), [(cinnamyl)PdCl]2 (1.0 mol %, 0.002 mmol), dodecane (25 μL, 0.55
mmol), K3PO4 (0.4 mmol), 2-Br-p-xylene (28 μL, 0.2 mmol) and o-cresol
(31.mg, 0.24 mmol). The vessel was evacuated and backfilled with argon
(this process was repeated a total of three times), after which toluene
(0.5 mL) was added via syringe . The solution was stirred at room
temperature for 16 h after which an aliquota was removed and filtered
through a pad of silica gel (eluted with ethyl acetate). Yields were
determined by GC employing dodecane as the internal standard.
1,4-dimethyl-2-(o-tolyloxy)benzene (11), yield 9%. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 7.29 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 7.16 (dd, J = 10.6, 4.4 Hz, 2H), 7.05
(t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 6.88 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 6.76 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H),
6.61 (s, 1H), 2.35 (s, 3H), 2.29 (d, J = 3.8 Hz, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (101
MHz, CDCl3) δ: 155.6, 155.2, 137.2, 131.4, 131.2, 128.9, 127.2, 125.9,
124.0, 123.0, 118.7, 117.7, 21.25, 16.4, 15.9 ppm. IR (neat, cm-1): 3024,
2923, 2361, 2338, 1684, 1653, 1619, 1577, 1506, 1490, 1457, 1408, 1379,
1302, 1254, 1227, 1185, 1148, 1121, 1042, 996, 939 cm-1. Anal. Calcd. for
C15H16O: C, 84.87; H, 7.60. Found: C, 84.97; H, 7.65.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM GC yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A New Biarylphosphine Ligand for the Pd-Catalyzed Synthesis of Diaryl
Ethers under Mild Conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Salvi, Luca; Davis, Nicole R.; Ali, Siraj Z.; Buchwald, Stephen L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(1), 170-173

