$DATUM Compound 30 Compound 29 (5.4 mg, 5.0 μmol) was combined with vacuum oven
dried K2CO3 (6.9 mg, 50 μmol, 10 equiv), 18-crown-6 and 4Å molecular
sieves (each ca 5 mg) in a round-bottom flask equipped with a reflux
condenser. The flask containing the solids was evacuated and refilled
with nitrogen. Freshly distilled THF (5.0 mL) was added, and the vessel
was warmed at 60 °C. After 12 h, the reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature, diluted with EtOAc (10 mL), and poured into a separatory
funnel containing aqueous 1 N HCl (10 mL). The aqueous layer was
extracted with EtOAc (10 mL × 2), and the combined organic layer was
washed with H2O (15 mL) and saturated aqueous NaCl (15 mL), dried over
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. Flash column chromatography
(SiO2, CH2Cl2:MeOH = 100:1 to 20:1) gave 30 (5.1 mg, 95%) as a mixture of
atropisomers (5:1). Analytical samples of each atropisomer were obtained
by PTLC (CH2Cl2:MeOH = 10:1) to give the major (M)-atropisomer and minor
(P)-atropisomer. This reaction was conducted on 110-330 mg scales
providing 30 in 70-90% yield. Compound 30, yield (5.1 mg, 95%) HRMS m/z
1079.1633 ([M+H]+, C48H46BrCl2N6O14 requires 1079.1627) IR (film) νmax
3306, 1659, 1534, 1514, 1491, 1353, 1230, 1165 cm-1 Major (M)-atropisomer
[α]23D -23 (c 0.2, MeOH). 1H NMR (THF-d8, 600 MHz) δ 8.38 (brs, 2H,
F6+ArOH), 8.17 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H, C-NH), 8.16 (d, J = 5.5 Hz, 1H, B2),
7.53 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H, F3), 7.38 (s, 2H, C2,6), 7.31 (dd, J = 8.4, 1.8
Hz, 1H, B6), 7.27 (brd, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H, F4), 7.19 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H,
B5), 7.08 (s, 1H, D6), 6.79 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H, A2,6), 6.70 (d, J = 8.4
Hz, 2H, A3,5), 6.49 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H, DNH), 5.84 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H,
A-NH), 5.75 (s, 1H, D2), 5.36 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H, D-α), 5.22 (d, J = 6.6
Hz, 1H, A-αH), 5.09 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H, C-α), 4.85 (dd, J = 12.0, 2.4 Hz,
1H, B-α), 3.60 (s, 3H, CO2Me), 3.37 (d, J = 13.8, 2.4 Hz, 1H, B-β2), 3.15
(dd, J = 13.8, 12.0 Hz, 1H, B-β1), 3.02 (s, 3H, B-NMe), 2.12 (s, 3H,
F-Ac), 1.33 (s, 9H, D-Boc) 13C NMR (THF-d8, 150 MHz) δ 171.7, 170.8,
170.7, 168.3, 168.0, 159.0, 156.2, 150.9, 149.9, 149.0, 144.2, 144.0,
139.6, 137.6, 137.4, 136.5, 132.5, 131.8, 131.4, 130.7, 130.6, 129.8,
129.1, 128.0, 127.6, 127.0, 126.4, 123.3, 123.2, 116.7, 116.2, 114.5,
79.2, 63.1, 57.0, 56.7, 53.9, 52.7, 34.0, 30.8, 28.7, 24.0 Minor
(P)-atropisomer [α]23D -48 (c 0.2, MeOH) 1H NMR (THF-d8, 600 MHz) δ 8.44
(d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1H, C-NH), 8.39 (s, 1H, F6), 7.83 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H,
B6), 7.77 (s, 1H, B2), 7.54 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H, F3), 7.39 (s, 2H, C2,6),
7.29 (m, 2H, B5+F4), 7.00 (s, 1H, D6), 6.77 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H, A2,6),
6.69 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H, A3,5), 6.18 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H, D-NH), 5.97 (s,
1H, D2), 5.81 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H, A-NH), 5.42 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H, D-α),
5.22 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H, A-α), 5.13 (d, J = 6.0, 1H, C-α), 4.85 (dd, J =
11.4, 3.0 Hz, 1H, B-α), 3.60 (s, 3H, CO2Me), 3.39 (dd, J = 14.4, 3.0 Hz,
1H, B-α), 3.17 (dd, J = 14.4, 12.0 Hz, 1H, B-β1), 3.01 (s, 3H, B-NMe),
2.11 (s, 3H, F-Ac), 1.36 (s, 9H, D-Boc) 13C NMR (THF-d8, 150 MHz) δ
